Since 2023, I've had the pleasure of being a speaker coach for TEDxQUT. Focusing on stagecraft and how speakers become more comfortable on stage and creating harmony between their words and their bodies.

My role as a speaker coach is to go beyond words and get the speakers more comfortable in their own bodies. For many, speaking at Tedx is the largest audience they have spoken in front of.

Using techniques I've developed in acting and working with business and startup founders I am able to give the speakers permission to play and capitalise on the message they are trying to get across with their talks.

The outcome is a talk that resonates with audiences. One of the speakers', [Sarina Petersen](https://www.ted.com/talks/sarina_petersen_how_bluey_teaches_adults_to_be_playful_again), talk was selected by TED to display on their site and has over 400,000 views.
